// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(594.96pt, 842.04pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(504.58pt, 790.2pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 96.26pt, "Abstract:")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 126.74pt, "Frequency comb spectroscopy provides broadband access to molecular fingerprints with ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 147.38pt, "mode-defined spectral resolution. However, its deployment in non-cooperative gas ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 168.14pt, "sensing remains challenging because conventional implementations require cooperative ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 188.78pt, "reflectors or well-controlled optical returns. Here, we overcome this limitation by ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 209.54pt, "introducing a computational sensing scheme based on a mode-programmable optical ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 230.18pt, "comb and a high-sensitivity single-pixel detector. In our approach, a two-dimensional ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 250.85pt, "disperser and a high-speed digital micromirror device encode individual comb modes, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 271.61pt, "enabling broadband, mode-resolved spectral acquisition without relying on coherent ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 292.25pt, "detection. This architecture supports measurements through highly scattering media and ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 313.01pt, "from non-cooperative targets while retaining the core advantages of frequency-comb ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 333.65pt, "spectroscopy. Our method achieves picometer-level spectral resolution, a 10-nm (1.27-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 354.41pt, "THz) instantaneous bandwidth, single-photon sensitivity down to 10⁻⁴ photons per pulse, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 375.05pt, "and compressed spectral acquisition with 2.5% sampling for <10% reconstruction error. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 395.81pt, "These capabilities establish a powerful platform for diverse gas-sensing applications, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 416.47pt, "including remote environmental monitoring, industrial leak localization, and explosive-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 437.23pt, "threat detection. ")
]

// arXiv source page 3
#original-page(594.96pt, 842.04pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(504.58pt, 790.2pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 99.98pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 136.58pt, "Spectroscopic gas sensing in hazardous or inaccessible environments requires techniques ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 157.34pt, "capable of non-cooperative, broadband, high-resolution measurements [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(432.58pt, 157.34pt, "1-4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(448.54pt, 157.34pt, "], supporting ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 177.98pt, "applications from remote atmospheric monitoring [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(334.03pt, 177.98pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(340.03pt, 177.98pt, "] to standoff detection of industrial ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 198.74pt, "leaks and chemical hazards [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(225.05pt, 198.74pt, "4")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(231.05pt, 198.74pt, "]. However, most existing approaches remain ill-suited to ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 219.38pt, "such conditions [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(171.02pt, 219.38pt, "5")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(176.93pt, 219.38pt, "]. Fourier-transform and dispersive spectrometers (see Fig. 1a) are ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 240.02pt, "fundamentally limited by optical path length and grating size, restricting their achievable ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 260.81pt, "resolution and accuracy, while frequency-swept laser spectroscopy suffers from narrow ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 281.45pt, "instantaneous bandwidths that impede simultaneous multi-gas detection [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(436.9pt, 281.45pt, "6")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(442.9pt, 281.45pt, "]. ")
  #line-at(97.104pt, 316.25pt, "Alternatively, frequency comb spectroscopy offers a powerful platform for broadband, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 336.89pt, "high-resolution measurements [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(239.33pt, 336.89pt, "7, 8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(258.29pt, 336.89pt, "]. A prominent example is dual-comb spectroscopy ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 357.65pt, "(DCS) [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(125.18pt, 357.65pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(131.18pt, 357.65pt, "], which employs two combs composed of evenly spaced, narrow linewidth ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 378.29pt, "modes with absolute frequency traceability. By heterodyning two combs with slightly ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 399.05pt, "different mode spacings on a single-pixel detector (Fig. 1b), it enables Fourier-transform ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 419.71pt, "spectroscopy without moving parts, thereby eliminating conventional constraints on ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 440.47pt, "spectral resolution, accuracy, and acquisition speed [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(335.11pt, 440.47pt, "10-13")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(363.07pt, 440.47pt, "]. Leveraging these advantages, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 461.11pt, "DCS has been successfully applied to diverse gas-sensing scenarios, including open-path ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 481.75pt, "greenhouse-gas monitoring [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(221.57pt, 481.75pt, "14-16")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.53pt, 481.75pt, "], multispecies trace-gas detection [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(416.98pt, 481.75pt, "17")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(428.98pt, 481.75pt, "] and agricultural ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 502.51pt, "gas-flux analysis [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(173.3pt, 502.51pt, "18")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(185.33pt, 502.51pt, "]. Most recently, remote DCS sensing over a 113-km open path has ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 523.15pt, "been demonstrated [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(183.89pt, 523.15pt, "19")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(195.89pt, 523.15pt, "]. However, such applications remain constrained to cooperative ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 543.91pt, "targets, such as calibrated reflectors, because the two combs must maintain mutual ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 564.55pt, "coherence at the detector [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(211.85pt, 564.55pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(223.85pt, 564.55pt, "].  ")
  #line-at(97.104pt, 599.38pt, "In contrast, combining a broadband comb with dispersive elements, such as a virtually ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 620.02pt, "imaged phased array (VIPA) [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(229.49pt, 620.02pt, "21")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(241.49pt, 620.02pt, "] or multi-mode fibers [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(353.71pt, 620.02pt, "22")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(365.71pt, 620.02pt, "], provides a phase-insensitive ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 640.78pt, "alternative to frequency comb spectroscopy. However, these approaches rely on camera-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 661.42pt, "based detection, which struggles under photon-starved conditions [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(413.74pt, 661.42pt, "23")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(425.74pt, 661.42pt, "], such as remote ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 682.18pt, "sensing of low-reflectivity targets or operation through highly scattering media (e.g., fog, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 702.82pt, "dust, clouds). So far, comb-based techniques for non-cooperative spectroscopic sensing ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 723.58pt, "remain largely unexplored. ")
]

// arXiv source page 4
#original-page(594.96pt, 842.04pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 423.5pt), 85pt, 319pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(504.58pt, 790.2pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(97.104pt, 96.02pt, "In this work, we demonstrate mode-programmable computational comb spectroscopy, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 116.66pt, "enabling broadband, high-resolution measurements with a single-pixel detector for non-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 137.42pt, "cooperative sensing. Our approach delivers (1) comb-mode-defined resolution across a ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 158.06pt, "broad instantaneous spectral width, (2) single-photon-level sensitivity to weak echoes, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 178.82pt, "and (3) compressible spectral recovery from strongly scattering, diffusive targets. With ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 199.46pt, "these advantages, our technique is promising for the gas-sensing applications mentioned ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 220.22pt, "above. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 258.89pt, "Results ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 295.73pt, "Basic principle")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 610.42pt, "Figure 1. Principles of frequency comb spectroscopy. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 627.46pt, "a, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.184pt, 627.46pt, "Conventional spectroscopic sensing methods. M, fixed mirror. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 644.74pt, "b, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(96.144pt, 644.74pt, "Dual-comb spectroscopy based on multiheterodyne detection between two optical combs with slightly ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 662.02pt, "different mode spacings. High coherence between the two combs at the detector is required to resolve the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 679.18pt, "dual-comb beat notes. OF, optical frequency; RF, radio frequency.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 696.46pt, "c, ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.064pt, 696.46pt, "Mode-programmable frequency comb spectroscopy. In this scheme, by encoding the comb modes that ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 713.74pt, "probe the molecules and measuring only the intensity of the back-scattered light, a broadband, mode-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 731.02pt, "resolved spectrum can be reconstructed computationally. I, intensity; t, time. ")
]

// arXiv source page 5
#original-page(594.96pt, 842.04pt, (image("graphics/page-05.png", width: 5.5pt), 421pt, 483.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(504.58pt, 790.2pt, "5 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(97.104pt, 96.02pt, "As illustrated in Fig. 1c, our approach employs a mode-programmable frequency comb ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 116.66pt, "that allows for arbitrary spectral encoding on a mode-by-mode basis, as each comb mode ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 137.42pt, "can be independently selected for computational spectroscopic sensing. By using a series ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 158.06pt, "of designed mode combinations, a broadband and high-resolution spectrum can be ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 178.82pt, "reconstructed from the intensity response of a single-pixel detector that measures back-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 199.46pt, "scattered light. The underlying principle is analogous to that of computational imaging ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 220.22pt, "[")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(89.184pt, 220.22pt, "24, 25")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(122.18pt, 220.22pt, "]: the measured signal is an encoded projection of the unknown spectrum. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 240.86pt, "Mathematically, the detection process can be expressed as ")
