  #line-at(96.984pt, 495.79pt, "Recently, single-photon DCS has been demonstrated for low-light detection in several ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 516.55pt, "works [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(121.1pt, 516.55pt, "30-37")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(149.06pt, 516.55pt, "]. A particularly relevant advance is single-photon dual-comb spectral ghost ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 537.19pt, "imaging [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(132.74pt, 537.19pt, "36")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(144.74pt, 537.19pt, "], which retrieves spectra by correlating dual-comb reference signals with ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 557.95pt, "single-photon counts. However, these approaches rely on mutually coherent dual combs ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 578.59pt, "and phase-sensitive multi-heterodyne detection performed under controlled environments. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 599.38pt, "They also require acquiring dual-comb interferograms over long time windows, yielding ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 620.02pt, "substantial data volumes that burdens real-time processing [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(369.79pt, 620.02pt, "38")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(381.79pt, 620.02pt, "]. In contrast, our approach ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 640.78pt, "operates without reference spectra and employs a single mode-programmable comb with ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 661.42pt, "intensity-only detection, enabling data-efficient, broadband, mode-resolved spectroscopy ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 682.18pt, "under non-cooperative conditions. ")
  #line-at(96.984pt, 716.86pt, "In fact, combining a comb with a VIPA-based 2D dispersive spectrometer has long ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 737.5pt, "enabled high-precision, mode-resolved spectroscopy [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(343.39pt, 737.5pt, "21")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(355.39pt, 737.5pt, "]. As in these works, the spectral ")
]

// arXiv source page 15
#original-page(594.96pt, 842.04pt, (image("graphics/page-15.png", width: 428pt), 83.5pt, 85pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.94pt, 790.2pt, "15 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(85.104pt, 96.02pt, "resolution of our system is set by the comb mode spacing—and ultimately by the comb ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 116.66pt, "linewidth—rather than by the dispersive optics, provided that individual comb modes are ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 137.42pt, "fully resolved. Also, the absolute mode frequencies can be retrieved with high accuracy. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 158.06pt, "In our setup, the frequency accuracy is currently limited by the wavemeter (±10 MHz) ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 178.82pt, "used to calibrate the EO-comb seed laser. In principle, this can be improved to the ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 199.46pt, "intrinsic linewidth of the seed laser (<0.1 kHz), corresponding to a fractional uncertainty ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 220.22pt, "of 5×10⁻¹² at ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(156.26pt, 220.22pt, "f")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(159.62pt, 221.18pt, "cw")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(168.98pt, 220.22pt, "=193.4 THz. Distinct from prior VIPA–comb implementations, our ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 240.86pt, "scheme integrates the 2D disperser with a DMD for encoding the comb modes, allowing ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 261.65pt, "the use of a highly sensitive single-pixel detector in place of a camera. This architecture ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 282.29pt, "enables compressed sensing and single-photon sensitivity, both of which are crucial for ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 303.05pt, "time-consuming, low-light measurements. ")
  #line-at(96.984pt, 337.73pt, "These capabilities provide clear advantages for real-world gas-sensing applications. ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 358.37pt, "Particaularly, by retaining the metrological strengths of frequency comb spectroscopy, ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 379.13pt, "the method is promissing for precise identification and quantification of multiple gas ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 399.77pt, "species. Moreover, its ability to operate without target-side reflectors makes it uniquely ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 420.55pt, "suited for standoff sensing in hazardous or unstructured environments, including ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 441.19pt, "industrial leak localization, explosive chemical accident sites, and open-air paths where ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 461.95pt, "only diffuse returns are available. Furthermore, we foresee this technique being integrated ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 482.59pt, "into intelligent sensing platforms, including drones [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(352.99pt, 482.59pt, "39")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(364.99pt, 482.59pt, "] and satellites [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(449.5pt, 482.59pt, "40")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(461.5pt, 482.59pt, "], thereby ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 503.35pt, "significantly boosting their spectral analysis capabilities for remote monitoring of ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 523.99pt, "greenhouse gases and pollutants. Finally, we note that when combined with sensitivity-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 544.75pt, "enhanced techniques [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(203.21pt, 544.75pt, "41-43")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(231.17pt, 544.75pt, "], such as cavity-enhanced spectroscopy [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(459.46pt, 544.75pt, "44-46")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(487.42pt, 544.75pt, "] or ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 565.39pt, "photoacoustic spectroscopy [")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(226.49pt, 565.39pt, "47-50")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(254.45pt, 565.39pt, "], our method could also deliver high sensitivity for ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 586.18pt, "trace-gas analysis, although this aspect is not the focus of the present work. ")
  #line-at(96.984pt, 620.86pt, "In summary, we introduce a computational spectroscopic technique based on a mode-")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 641.5pt, "programmable comb, which combines high spectral resolution with broad simutaneous ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 662.26pt, "bandwidth (10 nm or 1.27 THz without spectral stitching), single-photon sensitivity, and ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 682.9pt, "the compressed, non-cooperative sensing ability. These capabilities position our approach ")
  #line-at(85.104pt, 703.66pt, "as a powerful tool for widespread gas sensing applications. ")
]

